      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Maximum daily dose:** Immediate-release metformin tops out at 2,550 mg/day in the US label. Some guidelines allow up to 3,000 mg/day. Extended-release tops out at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** Single doses are generally no more than 1,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest standard tablet strength for three-times-daily dosing.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- A total of 1,700 mg/day, for example 850 mg PO twice daily\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose."
      }
     ],
